* Device models for the power-button / BOOTSEL testbench.
*
* None of these are vendor SPICE models: CJ (CJ2101) publishes none, and the
* rest are fitted to the datasheet numbers they cite so every parameter
* traces to a page we have in design/datasheets/. Where a number is a
* datasheet LIMIT rather than a typical, the testbench sweeps it as a
* corner (run.py CORNERS) instead of trusting the fit.
*
* Corner parameters (overridden per run with .param):
*   vto_p    CJ2101 VGS(th)    ds: -0.45 min / -0.7 typ (no max given)
*   vto_p4   LBSS84WT1G VGS(th) ds: -0.8 / -2.0 (Q4; hot corner less 2mV/C)
*   vto_n    BSS138W VGS(th)   ds: 0.8 / 1.3 / 1.5
*   idss     BSS138W drain leak at 25C (A), x2 per ~15C (ElecSuper's 1uA@25C ->
*            100uA@125C max slope); hot corner = 1uA at 85C (review F2). A
*            judgment, not a limit: the spec is at 40-60V, real 4V parts are nA;
*            leakstudy.py's 3uA column bounds it.
*   vt_pos   LVC2G14 VT+ @3V   Nexperia ds Table 8: 1.30 / 1.76 / 2.20
*   vt_neg   LVC2G14 VT- @3V   Nexperia ds Table 8: 0.60 / 1.04 / 1.50
*   en_th    NCP730 EN rising  ds p.4: 0.7 / 0.9 / 1.05
*   en_hy    NCP730 EN hyst.   ds p.4: 0.01 / 0.1 / 0.2
*   en_pu    NCP730 EN pull-up ds p.4: 0.01 / 0.3 / 1 uA
*   ii       74LVC2G14 input leakage (A, + = into the pin): Nexperia +-1uA max
*   itvs     PESD5V0S1BL IRM at 25C: 5nA typ / 100nA max


* ---- MOSFETs (ngspice VDMOS: 3-terminal, body diode included) ----
* CJ2101 P-ch, SOT-323. RDS(on) 100m@-4.5V, 140m@-2.5V, 210m@-1.8V;
* Ciss 640p, Coss 120p, Crss 82p (ds p.2). ksubthres gives a real
* subthreshold tail, which is what the off-state leakage checks lean on.
* CALIBRATION: the datasheet defines VGS(th) at ID = -250uA. With Kp=3 and
* ksubthres=0.1 the model reaches 250uA 0.20V before its own Vto, so Vto is
* offset by -0.20V to make ID(vto_p) = 250uA. ksubthres=0.1 is ~117mV/dec,
* a pessimistic (hot) slope: at vto_p=-0.45 it gives ID(VGS=0, VDS=-4V)
* ~30nA, and ~0.4uA at the -0.33V hot corner, both inside IDSS <= 1uA (ds).
* (Uncalibrated, the -0.33V corner leaked ~25uA at VGS=0 and the latch
* "turned itself on" in simulation: a model artifact, not the circuit.)
.model CJ2101 VDMOS(pchan Vto={vto_p-0.2} Kp=3.0 Rd=0.03 Rs=0.01 Rg=5
+ Cgs=560p Cgdmax=150p Cgdmin=40p Cjo=120p Is=1e-11 N=1.2 ksubthres=0.1)

* LBSS84WT1G P-ch, SOT-323 (Q4 since review F2). VGS(th) -0.8 / -2.0V @250uA
* (corner vto_p4), RDS(on) 2 typ / 6 max @-5V (model ~3), Ciss 38p, Crss 2.7p
* (ds p.2). CALIBRATION: with Kp=0.14 / ksubthres=0.1 the model reaches 250uA
* 0.02V before its Vto (gate tied to drain, as the ds test), so Vto is offset
* by -0.02V to make ID(vto_p4) = 250uA.
.model BSS84W VDMOS(pchan Vto={vto_p4-0.02} Kp=0.14 Rd=0.5 Rs=0.5 Rg=10
+ Cgs=35p Cgdmax=5p Cgdmin=2p Cjo=5p Is=1e-12 N=1.2 ksubthres=0.1)

* BSS138W N-ch, SOT-323. VGS(th) 0.8-1.5V, RDS(on) ~3.5 ohm @4.5V,
* Ciss ~27p (BSS138 family datasheets). Calibration: ID(Vto) = 288uA at
* VDS 4V with these parameters, i.e. Vto already sits at the 250uA point.
.model BSS138W VDMOS(nchan Vto={vto_n} Kp=0.12 Rd=0.5 Rs=0.2 Rg=10
+ Cgs=22p Cgdmax=8p Cgdmin=2p Cjo=12p Is=1e-12 N=1.1 ksubthres=0.1)

* ---- diodes ----
* Reverse leakage IS modelled, through each model's IS and its temperature
* scaling (EG, XTI), calibrated to the datasheet reverse-current curves at
* the ~4V reverse bias these parts see on this board:
*
* DSI: BAV70W (D4) / BAV99W (D2) / 1N4148WS (D5) silicon switching diodes,
* all IR <= 25-30nA @20-25V at 25C in their datasheets. 1N4148 forward
* set: VF = 0.58V @1mA, ~0.43V @30uA (Diodes DS30063 Fig. 2; VF max 0.715V
* @1mA). IR = IS = 2.5nA at 25C (ds max 25nA @20V); EG=0.85 puts 85C at
* ~1.1uA, matching the ds trend (25nA @25C -> 30uA @150C, ~x1.8 per 10C).
* (EG=1.11 would claim ~6uA at 85C, ~8x pessimistic.)
.model DSI D(Is=2.52n N=1.752 Rs=0.568 Cjo=2p Bv=100 Ibv=100u Eg=0.85 Xti=3)
* BAT54 Schottky (D2 = BAT54SW). VF 0.24V @0.1mA, 0.32V @1mA (Nexperia
* Table 7). IR: ~0.15uA @25C -> ~20uA @85C with Schottky EG=0.69/XTI=2,
* matching Nexperia BAT54W Fig. 2 (~0.3uA / ~20uA typ at 4V).
.model BAT54 D(Is=1.5e-7 N=1.05 Rs=2.5 Cjo=10p Bv=30 Ibv=2u Eg=0.69 Xti=2)
* B5819WS 1A Schottky (D3). VF ~0.3V @60mA. IR: ~2uA @25C -> ~130uA @75C,
* matching Yangjie B5817WS-B5819WS Fig. 4 (~3uA @25C, ~120uA @75C at 10%
* of rated VR = 4V). design/datasheets/B5819WS_yangjie.pdf
.model B5819 D(Is=2e-6 N=1.05 Rs=0.08 Cjo=110p Bv=40 Ibv=1m Eg=0.69 Xti=2)

* 1N4007WS (D3 since 2026-10-24), MDD ds design/datasheets/1N4007WS_MDD.pdf.
* Forward fit to Fig. 3 (typ, 25C): 0.80V @0.1A, 0.97V @1A -> Is 4n, N 1.8,
* Rs 0.08; EG 1.0 gives Fig. 3's ~-1.3mV/C. Reverse current is NOT the
* diode's Is here (that would be the forward fit's 4nA): Fig. 2 shows a
* generation-type leak, ~0.02uA @25C and ~0.6uA @75C at low VR, i.e. x2
* per ~10C, so it is a separate temperature-scaled source (temper = the
* simulation temperature). 85C -> ~1.2uA + Is(85C) ~0.26uA.
.model D4007F D(Is=4n N=1.8 Rs=0.08 Cjo=5p Bv=1000 Ibv=5u Eg=1.0 Xti=3)
.subckt D4007WS A K
D1 A K D4007F
Blk K A I = 20n * exp((temper - 25) / 14.6) * tanh(V(K,A) / 0.1)
.ends D4007WS

* PESD5V0S1BL bidirectional TVS (D6), Nexperia ds Table 6: VBR 5.5-9.5V
* @1mA, VCL <=10V @1A and <=14V @12A (8/20us), Cd 35pF. Symmetric smooth
* clamp, knee 7.5V + 0.4 ohm: ~7.5V @1mA, ~7.9V @1A, ~12.3V @12A.
* (Not two anti-series diodes: their midpoint is an internal node that
* starts at 0V under uic, i.e. 3.4V forward on one diode at t=0.)
* Leakage: corner param itvs = IRM at 25C (5nA typ, 100nA max), scaled by
* Fig. 6's typical temperature slope (x2 per ~17C: x11.5 from 25 to 85C).
* tanh() makes it the full IRM from ~0.4V up, i.e. no credit for running at
* 4V instead of the 5V test voltage.
.subckt PESD5V0S1BL A B
Bcl A B I = 0.05 / 0.4 * (ln(1 + exp(min((V(A,B) - 7.5) / 0.05, 60))) + max((V(A,B) - 7.5) / 0.05 - 60, 0)
+ - ln(1 + exp(min((-V(A,B) - 7.5) / 0.05, 60))) - max((-V(A,B) - 7.5) / 0.05 - 60, 0))
Blk A B I = {itvs} * exp((temper - 25) * 0.04077) * tanh(V(A,B) / 0.2)
C1 A B 35p
.ends PESD5V0S1BL

* ---- switch model for the B3U contact: 100 mohm max closed (ds),
* 100 Mohm min insulation (ds) ----
.model SWB3U SW(Vt=0.5 Vh=0.05 Ron=0.1 Roff=100Meg)

* ---- hysteretic comparator building block ----
* out = 1 when in rises above vhi, 0 when it falls below vlo. The state is
* fed back through a 1k/1n RC so the netlist has no algebraic loop, and the
* edge is smooth enough for the solver.
.subckt HYSCMP in out vhi=1 vlo=0.5
B1 s0 0 V = (V(in) > (V(out) > 0.5 ? {vlo} : {vhi})) ? 1 : 0
R1 s0 out 1k
C1 out 0 1n
.ends HYSCMP

* ---- NCP730 3.3V LDO (behavioral) ----
* EN comparator: rising en_th, falling en_th-en_hy. EN pull-up current (SPICE: a
* source "n+ n- I" pushes I out of n-, i.e. into EN)
* en_pu to IN (ds: "flowing out of the chip"). UVLO 1.95V rising / 0.2V hyst.
* Soft start ~0.5ms. Dropout 290mV @150mA -> ~2 ohm. Sources only (no
* sink), so the output caps discharge through the load, as in the part.
.subckt NCP730 OUT GND EN IN
XEN EN en_ok HYSCMP vhi={en_th} vlo={en_th-en_hy}
XUV IN uv_ok HYSCMP vhi=1.95 vlo=1.75
BPU GND EN I = {en_pu} * (V(IN) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0) * (V(EN) < V(IN) ? 1 : 0)
Bref r0 GND V = 3.3 * V(en_ok) * V(uv_ok)
Rss r0 ref 1k
Css ref GND 0.5u
Bout GND OUT I = max(0, min(0.25, 2.0 * (min(V(ref), V(IN) - 0.05) - V(OUT))))
Riq IN GND 2.5Meg
.ends NCP730

* ---- LGS4056H charger (behavioral) ----
* CC 50mA (R8 18k) while VCC > BAT + 0.1V and VCC > 3.9V, tapering into
* CV 4.20V. Only the presence/absence of charge current matters here.
.subckt LGS4056H VCC BAT GND
Bchg GND BAT I = (V(VCC) > 3.9 ? 1 : 0) * (V(VCC) > V(BAT) + 0.1 ? 1 : 0)
+ * max(0, min(0.05, 0.5 * (4.2 - V(BAT))))
Rq VCC GND 10Meg  $ unpowered VCC is high-Z (review N3; 100k flattered VBUS)
.ends LGS4056H

* ---- 74LVC2G14 one gate (behavioral) ----
* Schmitt inverter. VT+ vt_pos / VT- vt_neg are the Nexperia Table 8 limits at
* VCC = 3V; they are scaled by VCC/3 here so the gate behaves while VCC
* ramps (the real thresholds fall with VCC too: 0.3-0.7V at 1.65V).
* Output = VCC * (not state) through 25 ohm (VOL 0.4V @16mA, ds).
* Below VCC ~1V the output is held low (unpowered: Ioff = output disabled).
* Input leakage: corner param ii (A), positive = current INTO node A
* (Nexperia 74LVC2G14 Table 7: II +-0.1uA typ, +-1uA max; TI's is +-5uA).
* VT+/VT- limits are identical in the Nexperia (Table 8) and TI datasheets.
.subckt LVC14 A Y VCC GND
Bii GND A I = {ii} * (V(VCC) > 1.0 ? 1 : 0)
Bs s0 GND V = V(A) > (V(st) > 0.5 ? {vt_neg} : {vt_pos}) * max(V(VCC), 0.1) / 3.0 ? 1 : 0
Rs s0 st 1k
Cs st GND 1n
By y0 GND V = (V(VCC) > 1.0 ? V(VCC) : 0) * (1 - V(st))
Ry y0 Y 25
.ends LVC14
